  },
  {
    "id": "session-42-i-believe-i-can-fly_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 42 - I Believe I Can Fly",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"42 - I Believe I Can Fly.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-42-1QdpT1FX4g7Um7ve3N25a1eKCQcHvjKZ6.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1QdpT1FX4g7Um7ve3N25a1eKCQcHvjKZ6\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"42 - I Believe I Can Fly.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QdpT1FX4g7Um7ve3N25a1eKCQcHvjKZ6/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "2",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-42-i-believe-i-can-fly_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "In Session 42, titled I Believe I Can Fly, the party stood at the edge of a jungle pit on Sciogost, seeking a path off the prisoner island that avoided the heavily guarded prison. A great flowering vine rose, swallowed Rhody, Albross, and Kibbit, and was finally destroyed by Maw’s arrows, sending the companions tumbling into the tunnels below where they rested and learned of Kibbit’s tragic past. Deeper in they met Zeldrigos the Indomitable Serpent, a dragon of living jacinth who claimed the island, kept Maw as collateral, and gave them a bag of wind to confront the storm witch Esadi the Herrying in her cloud tower. The bag carried them to a marble platform where closing a suspicious censer transported them into rooms of living paintings, an Iron Golem, and a fountain of gold guarded by animated weapons. The session ended with the party split between chambers, the golem momentarily inert, and no clear way to reunite.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "3",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-41-the-mighty-jungle_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 41 - The Mighty Jungle",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"41 - The Mighty Jungle.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-41-13dvMS4yNXmttBq79Hkp6zO5DtzvXerBN.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"13dvMS4yNXmttBq79Hkp6zO5DtzvXerBN\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"41 - The Mighty Jungle.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/13dvMS4yNXmttBq79Hkp6zO5DtzvXerBN/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "4",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-41-the-mighty-jungle_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The teleported group found themselves stranded on a rocky shore under dark rain and fog, nowhere near Gevakaln, and set out to learn where they were and how to escape. A living vine and acid-spitting giant lizard nearly killed Pagern before Rhody and the others drove the lizard off and met Kibbit, a goblinoid who revealed they stood on Scidogost, the notorious prisoner island. Albross’s patron pointed them toward the jungle while chatty Jamaican trees spoke of a Lord of the Jungle who had brought them to life. After a short rest the party chose the jungle over the prison, survived a giant snake ambush, and ended the session peering into a cave pit where a large vine rose to meet them, its flower blooming in the same strange colors as the bonsai above.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "5",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-40-zeroes-of-khagdaruhl_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 40 - Zeroes of Khagdaruhl",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"40 - Zeroes of Khagdaruhl.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-40-173-7EE7PBlCL6DQ8asfrpvfkn7vIPaQ4.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"173-7EE7PBlCL6DQ8asfrpvfkn7vIPaQ4\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"40 - Zeroes of Khagdaruhl.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/173-7EE7PBlCL6DQ8asfrpvfkn7vIPaQ4/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "6",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-40-zeroes-of-khagdaruhl_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party fought to place the Rimestone on its pedestal and reseal the eldritch threat beneath the throne room. Lucerion returned from a harrowing vision, the party battered Admiral Xezev with critical strikes and fire, and the Rimestone’s blinding light knocked everyone unconscious for three days; they awoke frozen in ice, Rhody dead once more, and the Sacred Crows chiseling them free. After the Lord Emperor summoned clerics and a grand celebration, he granted Khagdaruhl’s neutrality, a tower anywhere in Orbansia, and the nearly complete legendary sword Kretopolus to Lucerion. Albross confirmed Rhody’s Feywild contract still bound his soul while visions showed Madam Mabel and a unicorn returning him to life; the party then contacted Saildreith the Copper Dragon and Lady Phéhldra Lightgarde about the orc threat to Nurador. An experimental Teleport scroll misfired, stranding Caelion, Albross, Rhody, Pagern and Maw on an unknown beach while Lucerion, Armaros and Kotio appeared on a hill overlooking Nurador and its orc encampments as the session ended.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "7",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-39-why-d-you-wanna-hit-me-man_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 39 - Why’d You Wanna Hit Me Man?",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"39 - Whyd You Want to Hit Me.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-39-1otVO4tOpcVmMmmaSLpkp4ZhY6MOJDos4.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1otVO4tOpcVmMmmaSLpkp4ZhY6MOJDos4\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"39 - Whyd You Want to Hit Me.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1otVO4tOpcVmMmmaSLpkp4ZhY6MOJDos4/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "8",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-39-why-d-you-wanna-hit-me-man_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party had to restore Rhody to life before returning to Khagdaruhl with the Rimestone to reseal the eldritch threat before its roots claimed more minds. In the dwarven kingdom, the group had time to rest and shop, learning of the legendary sword Kretopulus, which with the party had two shards from and which they handed to forgemaster Hultgrum for restoration.  Lucerion attuned to the Rimestone hoping to drive back a blizzard that had already started across the land, and then the group went to seal back the threat under the throne room.  Inside they faced Admiral Xezev, a twelve-foot insectoid Astral Plane servant who demanded the Rimestone be placed to free his master; combat erupted with memory-modifying grabs, possession of Lucerion that sparked chaotic friendly fire and fireballs, ending with Lucerion dropped and the Admiral reappearing above his body as the session closed.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "9",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-38-just-the-tip_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 38 - Just the Tip",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"38 - Just the Tip.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-38-1kgl8dEcbCV-VZl4YZffWuDk36yST6ChW.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1kgl8dEcbCV-VZl4YZffWuDk36yST6ChW\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"38 - Just the Tip.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kgl8dEcbCV-VZl4YZffWuDk36yST6ChW/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "10",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-38-just-the-tip_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party arrived at Master Icy Sow’s building to find the Sacred Crows victorious over the monks, claimed the last amulet fragment along with a \\+2 scimitar and the revelation that Pagern’s staff was a Staff of Frost, then struck the assembled necklace to open a spiraling pit and navigated the ice-sealed halls below. In the Room of Detachment they bought rest through sacrifice, solved the deadly elemental bell puzzle in the Room of Bells, felled Dearth the black fox mount of the Cold Breath, and faced Huldi himself in a vast chamber of plummeting platforms where ice blades, a wall-bursting eldritch horror, and a shattered blade led to Pagern’s killing blow, Rhody’s death and Caelion’s Revivify, the Sacred Crows’ arrival, and Lucerion claiming the Rimestone as the platform rose into warmer air, the session ending with the immediate threat ended yet the aberration’s presence still looming.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "11",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-37-taking-the-fight-to-iohir_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 37 - Taking the Fight to Iohir",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"37 - Taking the Fight to Iohir.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-37-1tzwRM6aDpPNILT507cp5xlDthzbHPxAV.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1tzwRM6aDpPNILT507cp5xlDthzbHPxAV\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"37 - Taking the Fight to Iohir.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tzwRM6aDpPNILT507cp5xlDthzbHPxAV/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "12",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-37-taking-the-fight-to-iohir_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party left the Rimestone room that was beneath the throne to Kahgdaruhl to report their findings to the Lord Emperor Thundermaul VI.  The irate dwarven king asked them to pursue the monks, having his guards escort them through an Arcane Waypoint to Iohir Monastery.  They stepped through the teleportation circle into a blizzard atop islands suspended above grinding ice. Rhody's Locate Object revealed the Rimestone beneath them marked by a snowflake on a great bell. Splitting from their allies, they confronted Master Polar Snake, whose lesson turned deadly with walls of ice and cones of cold until the party's blades and fireballs brought him low and claimed several snowflake amulet pieces. They secured more fragments from the next building, then faced the Hand of the Cold Breath who summoned a translucent brother and kicked Albross into the freezing waters below, only to be felled after by Lucerion’s Channel Divinity.  Rescuing their companion, the party reached Master Icy Sow's building where the Sacred Crows already waited.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "13",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-36-audience-with-the-lord_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 36 - Audience with the Lord",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"36 - Audience with the Lord.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-36-1ESlSUH6oHwa5segtxSwJZvearbjVRGAo.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ESlSUH6oHwa5segtxSwJZvearbjVRGAo\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"36 - Audience with the Lord.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ESlSUH6oHwa5segtxSwJZvearbjVRGAo/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "14",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-36-audience-with-the-lord_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party entered Khagdaruhl's Great Hall with one clear purpose: secure an alliance with Witguard and permission to examine the Rimestone while warning the Lord Emperor of its theft by Master Huldi and the Cold Breath.  The Lord Emperor confirmed the monks' strained ties, revealed the Rimestone's ancient purpose of freezing an undead aberration awakened by dark magic in the once-verdant Yagvur Sierra, and allowed them to descend as Runegrip representatives. In the frozen depths they battled an eldritch entity after a deceptive Sending reply, enduring place-swaps, universe-spanning visions, and stellar fury until Caelion's Spirit Guardians tore the creature apart, though the session closed on the chilling realization that the Cold Breath's actions had already set something far more cunning loose beneath the mountain.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "15",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-35-bloody-endeavor-civil-war_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 35 - Bloody Endeavor: Civil War",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"35 - Civil War.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-35-1Rog20hvD9EQR7pJoh7_xm5v07DHPi-vH.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1Rog20hvD9EQR7pJoh7_xm5v07DHPi-vH\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"35 - Civil War.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Rog20hvD9EQR7pJoh7_xm5v07DHPi-vH/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "16",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-35-bloody-endeavor-civil-war_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "They stepped into the Ring of Respect to face the Sacred Crows and earn an audience with Lord Emperor Thundermaul the Sixth. The arena dissolved into combat and after four bruising rounds, Wyrm Bane stood triumphant amid thunderous applause. The gained access to Khagdaruhel after some rest and healing, where they did library research on the city’s lords, and used a Sending spell warning Albross’s brother Breemos about his looming kidnapping all followed in swift order. The companions ended the session being escorted into the magnificent Hall of the Mountain King, poised at last for their imperial audience.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "17",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-34-greatest-of-all-time_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 34 - Greatest of All Time",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"34 - Greatest Of All Time.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-34-1A8SE6fWLFUsuq55K7STfiy89hluwVTV4.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1A8SE6fWLFUsuq55K7STfiy89hluwVTV4\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"34 - Greatest Of All Time.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A8SE6fWLFUsuq55K7STfiy89hluwVTV4/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "18",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-34-greatest-of-all-time_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "Pressing into the Vanapur Mountains, the group had one gloriously goal: retrieve the brown braided blind goat. They burst into a posh bedchamber, dispatched a sword-waving drow and causing Madam Mizna Er’Arachna to surrender.  With the goat safely recovered by the Sacred Crows and both towers cleared, the group traveled underground to the gem-studded cavern kingdom of Khagdaruhel, where Pagern tried to unsuccesfully buy a mage tower. Ambassador Greythane revealed the Rimestone’s broken prison and monk Huldi Coldbreath’s ambitions before sending the party into the Ring of Respect. There they bested hell hounds and the deadly Zhis’ta the Purple, ending the session on the very brink of their final bout against the Sacred Crows.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "19",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-33-caw_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 33 - Caw\\!",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"33 - Caw.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-33-1KI5YrQk-LMUjGn0aZ2VOcvfyu2nfHhMG.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1KI5YrQk-LMUjGn0aZ2VOcvfyu2nfHhMG\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"33 - Caw.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KI5YrQk-LMUjGn0aZ2VOcvfyu2nfHhMG/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "20",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-33-caw_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "Descended from the Vanapur Mountains toward Khagdaruhel, the party were still commited to geting the dwarves support and they wanted to investigate rumors of the Cold Breath’s growing influence on the Rimestone. Along the way they encountered the Sacred Crows, a capable adventuring group, who had been stalled outside Khagdaruhel searching for a missing blind goat beloved by a dwarven knight. The two parties formed a temporary alliance, tracked the goat to a foul cave occupied by an elder ettin.  Dispatching the giant, they pressed deeper to discover ancient dwarven towers now held by drow bearing banners of fangs and webs. In a coordinated assault on the towers, the combined force battled through the drow and a venomous spider-like boss that webbed and struck from the shadows.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "21",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-32-over-the-edge_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 32 - Over the Edge",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"32 - Over the Edge.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/bloody-endeavor/session-32-1yAL3NE_XnavPtpAbFPuuBXr8CNL_K-9j.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1yAL3NE_XnavPtpAbFPuuBXr8CNL_K-9j\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"32 - Over the Edge.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yAL3NE_XnavPtpAbFPuuBXr8CNL_K-9j/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "22",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-32-over-the-edge_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
